1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:12,084
This is the blacksmith, the computational workhorse. It loads the data, engineers the features, trains and evaluates the models, and builds the apps you explore results in.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:22,005
Its file lists the work. Load and preprocess data in any common format. Engineer features, handle class imbalance, make the splits.

3
00:00:22,005 --> 00:00:32,275
Train and tune classifiers, evaluate them with the right metrics, and leave clean, commented code behind so the run can be repeated.

4
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:44,434
Publication figures are the artist's; its own plots are quick diagnostics. Methodological validation is the adversary's: it does not mark its own homework as sound.

5
00:00:44,434 --> 00:00:52,800
And it does not write to the immutable data root. Outputs go under append only, versioned, never overwriting.

6
00:00:53,199 --> 00:01:04,424
A real run, on simulated data. The adversary had found a confound, so the member asks the blacksmith for the within-country differences and a stratified permutation test.

7
00:01:04,424 --> 00:01:16,848
The verdict is Done, with the numbers: the effect survives stratification, and the caveat that the countries do not agree. The results file and the code are named.

8
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:27,777
To use it, type to Claude Code and name it: ask the blacksmith to compute, train or build something. Give it the data, what to predict and where outputs go.

9
00:01:27,777 --> 00:01:44,287
The first line is the verdict: Done, Failed or Partial. Then the numbers, the files it wrote and the code, so the adversary can re-run it. Send the result to the adversary before the PI.
